---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
const questions = [
  ['What runs without configuration?', 'The three core checks: comment length, file length on whole-file writes and additions, and inline GitHub PR/issue body length. Supported test-runner output is also filtered. Em-dash and AI-writing checks are disabled until you enable them.'],
  ['Does Concise rewrite my code?', 'No. It denies a supported tool call and gives the agent the exact finding. The agent can then submit a rewrite. The website examples illustrate that exchange; this website does not run an agent or change your files.'],
  ['What if I want to keep the text?', 'Style checks use confirm mode by default: resubmit the identical text to keep it. You can exempt a line with concise-ignore, allow a phrase, ignore a path, or enable softFail for flagged allows. Core checks and deny mode also have a retry escape after two denials on the same target.'],
  ['Does it scan the whole repository?', 'No. It checks the submitted write or added text in supported edit and patch calls. It does not rescan surrounding existing content. The 300-line limit applies to whole-file Write calls and patch Add File operations, not ordinary update hunks.'],
  ['Are the writing checks an AI detector?', 'No. They match configurable phrasing, punctuation, and text-statistics patterns. Human writing can trigger them, and generated writing can pass. Use exceptions and choose categories that fit your project.'],
  ['Which agents does it support?', 'Claude Code, Codex CLI 0.152.0 or newer, and omp. In Codex, review and trust each Concise hook under /hooks; Codex asks again after a hook definition changes. In omp, subagent replies are not checked.'],
];
---
<MarketingLayout title="FAQ — Concise" description="Answers about Concise defaults, retries, supported agents, optional writing checks, and what the hooks do and do not inspect.">
  <header class="page-intro frame"><h1>Useful answers</h1><p>What Concise checks, what it leaves alone, and how to keep intentional text.</p></header>
  <section class="faq-section frame page-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="faq-intro"><h2 id="faq-heading">Before you install.</h2><p class="faq-tail">A specific edge case? <a href="https://github.com/yannelli/be-concise/issues">Open an issue on GitHub.</a></p><p class="faq-tail">For exact host coverage, see <a href="/docs/tools/">supported tools</a> and <a href="/docs/host-features/">host features</a>.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-list">{questions.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}<span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
